        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat: retain iMessage tombstones and revisions",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- migrate young v0.1 archives to schema v2 with source-attributed tombstones on canonical and subordinate entities\n- make sync merge by default, bind archives to one normalized Messages source, and add explicit `sync --restore` replacement\n- retain stable message events plus Apple edit, partial-unsend, and full-unsend revision state from binary `message_summary_info`\n- keep tombstoned rows out of active reads and search while retaining orphan active messages\n\nThis brings imsgcrawl onto the crawler-family tombstone contract from its first release line, following the direction established in openclaw/slacrawl#92 and the notcrawl/graincrawl implementations.\n\n## Proof\n\n- `go mod verify`\n- `go test -count=1 ./...`\n- `go vet ./...`\n- `go run golang.org/x/tools/cmd/deadcode@v0.45.0 -test ./...`\n- Darwin production build plus Linux amd64 cross-build\n- real `bin/imsgcrawl` against fake scratch Messages databases:\n  - merge retained absent rows; repeat import kept event identities stable; restore replaced the archive\n  - binary plist edits, partial unsends, and full unsends produced the expected revision events and visibility\n  - explicit parent tombstones propagated source-specific reasons to subordinate rows\n  - legacy-schema merge retained known revision metadata; restore cleared unavailable fields\n  - blank-GUID messages retained independent tombstone state\n  - same normalized source path survived atomic file replacement; a different path required `--restore`\n- AutoReview clean with no accepted/actionable findings\n",
